  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Laundry Innovation in Household and Community Settings Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Partners for Water project focuses on improving water efficiency, health conditions, and environmental performance within Bangladesh&apos;s household and informal laundry sector, by&#x2022;	assessing current practices,&#x2022;	gendered workloads,&#x2022;	chemical exposure, and water use, and&#x2022;	co-designing low-cost, practical innovations with women&apos;s groups in rural and semi-urban areas.Through diagnostic fieldwork, pilot testing, stakeholder engagement, and alliance-building, the project will generate evidence on feasibility and impact, while developing a 2-5 year roadmap for inclusive scale-up and potential long-term investment engagement, contributing to strengthened water security, gender equity, and sustainable WASH systems.</narrative>
  </description>
